{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"179245f5590711570b3d049840a6cba84d601a85dc6e8eaa4cfb16d9be67ea4a","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_09cedb49ca5da47d5b95e845477f9d3b6a51bca020c702d661c173c20d03c217","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a technical contribution to machine comprehension using the SQuAD dataset. The supplied evidence is insufficient to determine specific policy compliance regarding anonymity, plagiarism, or broader impact documentation, as no frozen venue policies or external overlap data are available. The paper explicitly cites the SQuAD dataset and its creators, addressing data provenance, but does not contain a dedicated ethics or broader impact statement.","paper_id":"B1-q5Pqxl","paper_identity_sha256":"f0a3523c05db60e2bbdf762391461d827fcf15b4fadeee965368011497aa49c4","prompt_identity_sha256":"df3fbd675bb1f4938d6980714152c08639d533940a6e9305d07e95619010aec7","raw_response_sha256":"95b3b4611ca6d182648a3c9fe0d9de5ddbee607d24b7a47cef9863afbcfb5c8a","request_identity_sha256":"8460c033fab124b8a0852e338c2d72d8af5a706beb8f67ba423caf9dc0dd641a","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"246e42ed15511d2829c5c387e87312a72aba34e11eccfcf439d0ef8721f75d25","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not contain a dedicated section discussing ethical risks, fairness, bias, or potential harms associated with the machine comprehension model. The work focuses on technical performance metrics (exact match and F1 score) on the SQuAD dataset. No specific ethical mitigation strategies or discussions of dual-use concerns are visible in the provided text.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-024","SRC-032"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes the Stanford Question Answering Dataset (SQuAD) v1.1, noting that passages are derived from Wikipedia articles and questions were created by humans through crowdsourcing. The authors explicitly cite the original SQuAD paper (Rajpurkar et al., 2016) and acknowledge the dataset's provenance. No specific privacy violations or misuse of licensed data are evident in the text, as the dataset is a standard public benchmark.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The paper header explicitly lists the authors' names (Shuohang Wang, Jing Jiang) and their institutional affiliation (Singapore Management University), along with their email addresses. While this is standard for published versions, the supplied evidence does not include a frozen venue anonymity policy for the specific submission context to determine if this constitutes a double-blind violation. The visible identifiers are noted, but no policy compliance judgment can be made without the specific review policy.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The supplied evidence does not contain information regarding plagiarism, self-plagiarism, or dual submission. The paper cites prior work, including the authors' own previous work on match-LSTM (Wang & Jiang, 2016), which is properly attributed. Without external overlap data or a frozen plagiarism check, it is not possible to verify originality or detect duplicate submission.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement, a responsible AI checklist, or explicit documentation of IRB/ethics approvals. The acknowledgments section thanks individuals for technical assistance (testing on hidden test data, Dockerfile help) but does not address societal implications or compliance with specific policy obligations. The absence of these elements is noted, but without a frozen policy requirement, no specific compliance failure is declared.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"2de0a47ae8883309a8